UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Six of Pentacles represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Equilibrium"—the fair, high-integrity phase where the sovereign consciousness, having navigated the scarcity of the Five, establishes a mature, reciprocal flow of material and energetic resources. Moving beyond the desperate survivalism of the Five, the Six signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Philanthropist," where you have reached a level of stability that allows you to engage in the ethical distribution of your surplus, recognizing that the health of your own system is inextricably linked to the vitality of the ecosystem you inhabit. Visually depicted as a figure weighing coins on a scale and distributing them to those in need, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Reciprocity"—the realization that true material mastery is not measured by the accumulation of assets, but by the intelligence and justice of their circulation. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Resource Optimization," where you are running balanced-budget protocols that account for both your internal sustainability and your external impact. When the Six of Pentacles appears, your system is registering a "Fair-Exchange" status; you have resources to share or the humility to receive, and you are being invited to stop the "selfish-loop" of fear-based hoarding and instead participate in the natural, rhythmic ebb and flow of manifest abundance. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your generosity. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Fairness": ensuring that your interactions—both incoming and outgoing—are governed by an objective assessment of value, need, and contribution, rather than by egoic manipulation or sentimentality. To inhabit the Six of Pentacles is to master the art of "Strategic Distribution," recognizing that by choosing to facilitate the equitable flow of resources, you are effectively strengthening the very network that supports your own, sovereign material life.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Six of Pentacles appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Inequality," "Transactional-Corruption," or the catastrophic refusal to acknowledge the power imbalance in your current exchanges—a state where you are effectively "buying influence," "creating dependency," or "being exploited" because you have lost sight of the fundamental requirement for mutual respect and objective value. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "manipulative generosity" or "shameful debt" with "maintaining stability," even as your internal operating system is experiencing a total, non-recoverable decay of its integrity. You are essentially "distorting the market," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "look powerful" or "feel like a victim" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually maintain a fair, transparent exchange. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "magnanimous benefactor" or the "grateful recipient," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of unease, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency resentment, the experience of "strings-attached interactions," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your current exchanges are fundamentally dishonest. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of codependency"; you are obsessively trying to force an outcome that lacks genuine reciprocity, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final correction of your boundaries is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to stand in the truth of an honest exchange, you would be forced to acknowledge that your relationships—or your self-worth—were predicated on this very distortion. The reversed Six of Pentacles exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "being evaluated on merit," and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense of the "transactional mask" and face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self, you would be forced to acknowledge that your power-plays were a defensive response to your own, underlying sense of inadequacy. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these manipulative, power-imbalanced scripts, perform a brutal audit of your exchanges, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize the integrity of your fair-deal over the utility of your control. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical transparency—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "the power dynamic" over the vulnerability of "the equal exchange," and realizing that until you are willing to clean up your transactions, demand true equity, and exist in the raw, unadorned reality of your own, honest worth, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom prestige you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 48;
